v {xschem version=3.4.7 file_version=1.2

* LDO error amplifier -- symbol.
*
* Two-stage Miller-compensated OTA (PMOS input pair, NMOS mirror load,
* NMOS common-source second stage, self-biased from VDD). See
* design/error_amp.sch for the schematic and design/error_amp.md for the
* topology rationale and the offset / PSRR / current budgets.
*
* PORT ORDER IS THE SWAP-IN CONTRACT issue #8 ratified for the error amp
* (design/README.md, ldo_erramp_placeholder.sym):
*
*     INP INN OUT VDD VSS EN BG
*
* INP is the NON-inverting input (wired to FB in ldo_core), INN is the
* INVERTING input (wired to VREF). That polarity is what negative feedback
* around a PMOS common-source pass device requires -- do not flip it.
*
* The first five pins' *coordinates* are deliberately identical to
* ldo_erramp_placeholder.sym's, so replacing the placeholder instance in
* ldo_core.sch was a one-token symbol-name change with no rewiring.
*
* EN (issue #11) is APPENDED as a sixth pin, so the first five keep both
* their order and their coordinates. Issue #9 flagged the missing enable
* explicitly ("the ratified 5-port interface has no EN pin, so this cell
* draws bias current whenever VDD is present ... flagged to #11") and #11
* owns the shutdown-Iq row, so #11 makes the interface decision #9 deferred.
* Positional instantiations DO need the extra node -- ngspice errors on the
* node count rather than mis-wiring silently, and design/netlist.py --check
* re-asserts symbol-vs-schematic pin order on every export.
*
* BG (issue #55) is APPENDED as a seventh pin on the same principle: the
* first six keep their order and their coordinates. BG is the class-AB
* buffer's INPUT node (the gate of the source follower Mbuf that #51 added).
* Exporting it is what lets design/ldo_softstart.sch and design/ldo_ilimit.sch
* release that follower while they clamp PASS_GATE, instead of fighting a
* 150 um device they were never sized against. See design/error_amp.sch's
* "BG IS A PORT" note for the full rationale and the polarity contract.
}
G {}
K {type=subcircuit
format="@name @pinlist @symname"
template="name=x1"
}
V {}
S {}
E {}
